⚠ THIS COMMIT SWEPT ANOTHER LANE'S WORK, and the sweep was mine.

`discord-bot/src/commands/admin.rs` in this commit is NOT bounty work. It is the admin surface of
the treasury fuel-gauge repair — the new `/dregg admin treasury refuel:<usd>` operator key, and
`refuel_signal` split out of `run_treasury` as a pure fn so the REFUEL NOW alarm is drivable from a
genuinely drained tank.

I committed `discord-bot/src/commands/` as a DIRECTORY and caught a live lane's in-progress file
with it. The rest of that work landed separately as `1259679bf` ("treasury: the fuel gauge could not
fall, so the REFUEL alarm could not fire"), which carries the full flag day: a hosted run now
requires funded fuel and refuses with `FuelExhausted` when the tank cannot cover one run.

So the flag day for the refuel key is NOT findable from this commit's subject. It is here.

The lesson is narrower than 'be careful': COMMIT NAMED PATHS, NOT DIRECTORIES, in a shared tree.
AGENTS.md says commit only named paths and I read a directory as one.
